2. WHAT THIS SOFTWARE DOES

This software removes editing restrictions from Microsoft Word (.docx)
documents. A .docx file is a ZIP archive containing XML. When a document author
applies "Restrict Editing" in Word, Word records that choice as a
<w:documentProtection> element inside word/settings.xml. That element is an
instruction to Word, not encryption: the document's text is stored in readable
XML whether or not the element is present. This software removes that element
and rebuilds the archive.

The restriction is a courtesy lock. It signals the author's intent that the
document not be altered. It is not a security boundary and was never designed
as one.


3. WHAT THIS SOFTWARE DOES NOT DO

This software does NOT decrypt password-encrypted documents. Those use an
entirely different file format (an encrypted OLE compound file) and are
genuinely unreadable without the password. This software detects them and
refuses to proceed. It contains no password cracking, brute-force, or
cryptographic attack capability of any kind.


4. PERMITTED USE

You may use this software on documents you have the right to modify, including:

  (a) documents you created;
  (b) documents you own or administer;
  (c) documents you have the owner's permission to edit;
  (d) templates and forms you are authorised to adapt;
  (e) your own documents whose restriction password has been lost;
  (f) study of the OOXML file format and of this software itself.


5. RESTRICTIONS

You may NOT use this software to:

  (a) alter a document you have no right to alter;
  (b) modify contracts, agreements, records, invoices, transcripts,
      certificates, or any instrument another party relies on being unaltered;
  (c) defeat a restriction where doing so breaches a contract, a licence, an
      employment or academic policy, or any applicable law;
  (d) misrepresent an altered document as an original;
  (e) commit fraud, forgery, or any other unlawful act.

Removing a technical restriction does not grant permission. If you were not
entitled to edit a document before using this software, you are not entitled to
edit it afterwards. The absence of a lock is not consent.


